    spipe_lacks_context_mode_chunking_and_surfaces_2026-08-31, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: followed the doc's 2026-11-11 triage addendum (fund gap 1 first; gaps 2/3 are the analyzer -v2 contract release, gap 5 a separate security feature, gaps 4/6 owner funding calls). Implemented the doc's gap-1 acceptance: a chunk id in the SPipe document model and a snippet field on SearchHit. What existed: full BM25 pipeline at context-mode parity, smart_truncate_bytes, simple_pipe/simple_context surfaces; what was missing: any chunk/snippet document model (SearchDocument whole-file only, no snippet on SearchHit). Added src/lib/common/search/chunk.spl (~330 lines): SearchChunk (deterministic id doc/field#ordinal, 1-based per field), ChunkBudget/SnippetBudget, chunk_document_v1 (line-boundary greedy packing; oversized lines hard-split into byte-consecutive UTF-8-safe pieces that rejoin; fail-closed chunk_budget_exceeded/invalid_chunk_budget), snippet_for_chunk_v1 (bounded excerpt centered on first query-term occurrence, chunk-head fallback), attach_document_snippets_v1 (ranked hits in, same ranks with best-matching chunk snippet out). document.spl: SearchSnippet type; SearchHit gains snippet: SearchSnippet? (existing 3-arg of unchanged, new of_snippet/has_snippet; all existing call sites compile unchanged). __init__.spl exports; source_inventory.lock registered. Spec test/01_unit/lib/common/search/chunk_spec.spl 11/11 PASS (ids/budgets/rejoin, UTF-8-safe hard splits, fail-closed ceilings, snippet default/attached, excerpt windowing + head fallback, end-to-end rank preservation, unknown-doc pass-through); neighbours knowledge_contract 6/6, document_contract 2/2, frozen_contract_v2 16/16, provider_contract 1/1, top_k 1/1, query_contract 1/1, index_engine 17/17, search_adapter 7/7, search_response_distrust 6/6, index_engine_provider 5/5, query_exec_json_quote_non_ascii 2/2 all PASS. Notable finding recorded in chunk.spl header: text.len() counts CODEPOINTS while slice/index_of/bytes are byte-based (the common/token_budget.spl comment claiming len is BYTES is wrong - harmless there, ASCII); all budget math uses bytes().len(). Residuals per triage: gaps 2+3 (Porter/trigram) need the analyzer -v2 release; gaps 4+5 separately scoped; gap 6 owner funding call; wire projection deliberately unchanged (frozen section 14.11/14.12 hashes) - snippet/chunk_id ride the next wire version per the search owner. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/common/search/chunk_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/common/search/knowledge_contract_spec.spl"

